    "caption": "Nothing screams summer like a thirst-quenching watermelon smoothie. What’s even better is if it’s spiked with some refreshing rosé!\n\nUsing a medium-sized seedless watermelon, which you can grab fresh from #TheMarketplace, put together this drink a few hours before you plan to consume it. Since the watermelon comes seedless, you definitely save up on time.\n\nWhat’s great about this recipe is that you can enjoy it as a mocktail, as well! Just add more lemon-lime soda, or substitute the rosé with fruit juice, so that it’s kid-friendly, too. Bottoms up!\n\nServing Time: 4 hours and 30 minutes\nYield: 6 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n1 medium-sized seedless watermelon, peeled\n3 cups rosé wine \n2 cups frozen strawberries\n6 tbsps. lime juice \n6 tbsps. simple syrup\n2 cups lemon-lime soda \n6 scoops vanilla ice cream\n1/2 cup freeze-dried strawberries\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Slice the seedless watermelon into bite size pieces. Freeze for at least 4 hours.\n2. Pour out 1 1/2 cups of rosé wine into ice cube trays, then freeze for at least 4 hours as well.\n3. When both the watermelon and rosè ice cubes are firm, transfer into a blender with the remaining rosé wine, frozen strawberries, lime juice and simple syrup. Pulse until smooth and slushie-like.\n4. Diving into serving glasses, filling each glass only 3/4-full. Top each serving with a scoop of vanilla ice cream and lemon-lime soda. Sprinkle freeze-dried strawberries on top.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
